====================================================================================================
1  CALIBRATION -- C(L) simulated, and LAMBDA fixed so a RANDOM WALK finds ONE segment
====================================================================================================
   C(L)  at L = 8, 12, 24, 36, 72:  1.005  1.009  1.001  1.005  1.003
   SD(L) at L = 8, 12, 24, 36, 72:  0.700  0.725  0.734  0.746  0.749
   z = eff*sqrt(L) is ESSENTIALLY L-INDEPENDENT, which is why the score must NOT be
   weighted by L -- the first version's bug, and it drove LAMBDA to 126.
   LAMBDA = 16.29  ->  a random walk yields 1.00 segments on average (100% of paths get exactly 1)

